window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-b31f99909c8e2724"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"forecast-cash-flow\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">预测现金流</h1> <p>在可编辑的预测工作簿中找出流动性最低点。</p> <p>向 ChatGPT 提供现金流输入和模型约束，然后请它创建可编辑工作簿：保留来源数据的时间频率，标记安全现金余额被突破的情况，并显示哪些假设会造成现金压力。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>需要编制 13 周或月度现金预测的财务与运营团队。</li> <li>需要在一份工作簿中纳入收款、工资、供应商付款和营运资金假设的预测。</li> <li>在规划会议前审查现金可支撑时间、安全余额是否被突破以及情景驱动因素的团队。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>$spreadsheets</code></td> <td>构建可编辑的预测工作簿，将公式关联到假设，并为情景和输入缺口添加检查项。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">起步提示词</h2> <p>预测现金流</p> <p>建议模型：<code>gpt-6-luna</code> · 建议推理级别：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">请使用 $spreadsheets，根据我附上的源文件构建一份可编辑的现金流预测工作簿。\n\n在可用时，纳入期初现金、预期收款、工资、供应商付款、债务、税款、资本支出、营运资金项目和时间安排假设。保留来源数据的时间频率，无论是每周还是每月。\n\n请提供汇总视图，标出流动性最低点、最低期末现金余额，以及任何低于安全现金阈值的情况。请使用公式，方便我之后更改假设；在使用占位值前，先指出缺失的时间安排假设。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">智能体技能</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"introduction\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">简介</h2> <p>编制现金流预测时，你需要确保预测准确并符合企业的实际情况。你可以使用 ChatGPT 创建预测工作簿，然后在 ChatGPT 中检查和修改它。请附上现金流输入、运营假设和模型约束。如果输入位于 Google Drive 或其他已连接的数据源中，也可以提供文件引用。</p> <p><a id=\"make-the-forecast\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">制作预测</h2> <ol> <li>附上现金流输入、运营假设和模型约束。</li> <li>运行起始提示词，并要求生成可编辑的 <code>.xlsx</code> 工作簿。</li> <li>在 ChatGPT 中打开工作簿，并展开为全屏视图，以检查假设、公式、情景和汇总工作表。</li> <li>在同一聊天中继续调整收款、工资、供应商付款、增长或安全余额假设。</li> </ol> <p>工作簿出现在聊天中后，打开它并展开为全屏视图。检查时间安排假设、公式、情景和汇总工作表，然后要求 ChatGPT 从这份工作簿继续修改。</p> <p><a id=\"review-cash-pressure\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">审查现金压力</h2> <p>使用预测前，请让 ChatGPT 找出现金最低点、核对工作簿与来源输入，并列出需要复核的假设。</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Review the cash-flow forecast.\n\nTell me:\n\n- the first week or month cash drops below the safety balance\n- the liquidity low point\n- the main drivers of cash pressure\n- formulas or tabs that do not tie to the source inputs\n- assumptions that need human review\n- which scenario I should review before using this with the team\n\nFix safe formatting or formula issues, then list anything I should review manually.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">请审查现金流预测。\n\n告诉我：\n\n- 现金首次低于安全余额的是哪一周或哪一月\n- 流动性的最低点\n- 造成现金压力的主要因素\n- 哪些公式或工作表无法与来源输入核对一致\n- 哪些假设需要人工审阅\n- 在与团队使用这些内容之前，我应该先审查哪个情景\n\n修复可以安全处理的格式或公式问题，然后列出我应该人工审阅的事项。</div></div> <p><a id=\"run-a-scenario\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_9\">运行一个情景</h2> <p>在 ChatGPT 中检查完工作簿后，使用后续提示词，每次只更改一个情景驱动因素。</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Add a scenario where [collections slow by X days, payroll increases by X%, vendor payments move earlier, or bookings increase by X% with collection timing of N days].\n\nKeep the base case visible, update dependent formulas, and tell me how ending cash and the liquidity low point change.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">请添加一个情景：[collections slow by X days, payroll increases by X%, vendor payments move earlier, or bookings increase by X% with collection timing of N days]。\n\n保持基准情景可见，更新相关依赖公式，并告诉我期末现金和流动性最低点发生了什么变化。</div></div>","en":"<h1 id=\"forecast-cash-flow\">Forecast cash flow</h1> <p>Find the liquidity low point in an editable forecast workbook.</p> <p>Give ChatGPT cash-flow inputs and model constraints, then ask it to create an editable workbook that preserves the source cadence, flags safety-balance breaches, and shows which assumptions drive cash pressure.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Finance and operations teams building a 13-week or monthly cash forecast.</li> <li>Forecasts that need receipts, payroll, vendor payments, and working-capital assumptions in one workbook.</li> <li>Teams reviewing runway, safety-balance breaches, and scenario drivers before a planning meeting.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>$spreadsheets</code></td> <td>Build editable forecast workbooks, wire formulas to assumptions, and add checks for scenarios and input gaps.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Forecast cash flow</p> <p>Suggested model：<code>gpt-6-luna</code> · Suggested reasoning effort：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $spreadsheets to build an editable cash-flow forecast workbook from the attached source files.\n\nUse beginning cash, expected receipts, payroll, vendor payments, debt, tax, capex, working-capital items, and timing assumptions where available. Preserve the source cadence, whether weekly or monthly.\n\nInclude a summary view that flags the liquidity low point, the minimum ending cash balance, and any breach of the safety cash threshold. Use formulas so I can change assumptions later, and call out missing timing assumptions before using placeholders.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">Agent skills</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"introduction\">Introduction</h2> <p>When you are building a cash-flow forecast, you want to make sure it is accurate and reflects the reality of your business. You can use ChatGPT to help you create a forecast workbook that you can inspect and revise in ChatGPT. Attach the cash-flow inputs, operating assumptions, and model constraints. You can also use file references when the inputs live in Google Drive or another connected source.</p> <h2 id=\"make-the-forecast\">Make the forecast</h2> <ol> <li>Attach the cash-flow inputs, operating assumptions, and model constraints.</li> <li>Run the starter prompt and ask for an editable <code>.xlsx</code> workbook.</li> <li>Open the workbook in ChatGPT. Expand it into the full-screen view to inspect assumptions, formulas, scenarios, and the summary tab.</li> <li>Continue in the same chat to change collections, payroll, vendor payment, growth, or safety-balance assumptions.</li> </ol> <p>When the workbook appears in the chat, open it and expand it full-screen. Review the timing assumptions, formulas, scenarios, and summary tab, then ask ChatGPT to revise the same workbook from there.</p> <h2 id=\"review-cash-pressure\">Review cash pressure</h2> <p>Before using the forecast, ask ChatGPT to identify the low point, tie the workbook back to the source inputs, and list assumptions that need review.</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Review the cash-flow forecast.\n\nTell me:\n\n- the first week or month cash drops below the safety balance\n- the liquidity low point\n- the main drivers of cash pressure\n- formulas or tabs that do not tie to the source inputs\n- assumptions that need human review\n- which scenario I should review before using this with the team\n\nFix safe formatting or formula issues, then list anything I should review manually.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"run-a-scenario\">Run a scenario</h2> <p>After reviewing the workbook in ChatGPT, use follow-up prompts to change one scenario driver at a time.</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Add a scenario where [collections slow by X days, payroll increases by X%, vendor payments move earlier, or bookings increase by X% with collection timing of N days].\n\nKeep the base case visible, update dependent formulas, and tell me how ending cash and the liquidity low point change.\n</code></pre>"};
